From: pocket-debs <masterxq@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] daemon: messages of every modem, SIM of each message, send through a chosen SIM
Description:
 The daemon used the first modem only: SMS that arrived on the SIM of
 another modem (dual SIM phones with one ModemManager modem per SIM) were
 never stored, and every message was sent through the first modem.
 .
 ModemController handles the messages of every modem (also of modems that
 come later) and keeps the first modem as the default one (MMS and the data
 bearer stay on it). Each message stores the SIM (ICCID) it was received on
 or sent through (new column Messages.sim, migration
 2026-11-25-120000_message_sim). sendMessage takes the SIM to send an SMS
 through (empty: the default modem). The new method sims() lists the active
 SIM of every modem with its slot (PrimarySimSlot, read over D-Bus), name
 ("SIM <slot>", else the operator name) and icon (shared with plasma-nm and
 plasma-dialer in simidentitiesrc, class SimIdentities); simsChanged is
 signalled when the SIMs change.
Forwarded: no
License: as the patched files (GPL-2.0-only OR GPL-3.0-only OR LicenseRef-KDE-Accepted-GPL); new files simidentities.* LGPL-2.1-only OR LGPL-3.0-only OR LicenseRef-KDE-Accepted-LGPL
Last-Update: 2026-11-25
